{
  "rules": [
    "Uptrend underestimation at longer horizons: when the last 5–10 days show a clear rising trend, the model systematically underpredicts the back half of the 30d path (especially days ~20–30), missing late breakouts by ~+2 to +9 EUR.",
    "Excess mean-reversion bias: forecasts pull back toward ~67–69 even when realized prices trend away; in sustained rallies the model flattens too early instead of letting the level drift higher.",
    "Volatility compression: the model’s forecast range is too narrow; it misses tail moves (notably sharp upside extensions) and produces overly smooth trajectories versus realized outcomes.",
    "Horizon-dependent sign flip: near-term (days ~1–10) errors are small/mixed, but medium-term (days ~10–20) tends to be slightly high during pullbacks, while long-term (days ~20–30) is materially low during rallies—apply increasing positive adjustment with horizon when momentum is positive.",
    "Late-cycle breakout miss: if spot/last observation is making new 30d highs, add an explicit ‘breakout premium’ to days 15–30 (e.g., ramping +1 EUR at day 15 to +4–6 EUR by day 30) rather than reverting to the prior range."
  ]
}
